284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Accredited Counselors of Thailand \(ACT\) is an independent, non-profit initiative under the LEAF Foundation \(est. 2012\), dedicated to offering Thai national and resident counselors the opportunity to obtain certified accreditation according to international standards through an extensive registration process for individuals and organizations. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ACT exists to support registered and accredited counselors in Thailand and surrounding countries, as well as to elevate, empower, and educate members of the general public who have a special interest in the counseling field. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Through education, networking, and best practice sharing, ACT stimulates counselors in Thailand to uphold the highest standards of accountability in their counseling career. With five membership levels, counselors can continue to grow in experience and depth of knowledge, sharing their expertise as valuable members of the ACT community. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
