303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ACT accreditation is a credential granted by the Accredited Counselors of Thailand \(ACT\) to qualified counselors in Thailand who meet the criteria. The purpose of obtaining ACT accreditation is to legally and ethically provide counseling services. Accreditation demonstrates that the holder has met the educational, clinical, and ethical standards required to practice counseling competently and safely. Counselors can apply to be a registered or accredited counselor depending on their level of experience. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Additionally, ACT accreditation meets international counseling standards, widening the scope of opportunity for counselors in Thailand and possibly increasing opportunities to expand their practice abroad. Please note that while ACT is working towards transferable credits across the APAC region in the future, local laws and licensing rules always apply. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( )
/Pg 12 0 R
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A registered counselor refers to a professional who has met the standard requirements regarding education, training, and ethical standards in providing counseling services. Registration is essential as it enhances credibility, fosters trust with clients, and ensures that counselors operate within legal and professional boundaries.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (An accredited counselor goes one step further: this is a highly experienced counselor who has been practicing under supervision for at least five years and has made significant contributions to the field of counseling. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
