/T (5. Closing Notes: The purpose of closing notes is for counselors to evaluate the effectiveness of treatment. After the last session, provide the client with a form asking them general questions regarding their mental health, compare them with the Client Intake Form or notes from your first session to assess their progress and recovery. Additionally, it is also possible to ask clients to fill out the same form on their first session in order to gain a clear picture of their mental health before and after counseling. Suggested template for Closing Notes in Appendix 3.)
