/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (3. Supervision Notes: Supervisees must take supervision notes to maintain an accurate record of their supervision hours. These notes serve as an essential tool for documenting the content and progress of each supervision session, ensuring that the supervisee can integrate the feedback received. Additionally, these records are crucial for evidencing the fulfillment of supervision requirements, whether for certification, accreditation, or professional development. The notes should include a concise summary of the key topics discussed, insights gained, challenges addressed, and any action plans or goals set during the session. Proper documentation not only supports accountability but also aids in the supervisee's professional growth and development as a practitioner. Please refer to the Guidelines for Professional Language; for supervision notes, no academic citation is required and informal language is acceptable, as long as it is clear, respectful, and appropriate. See Appendix 6.5 for a template of Supervision notes.)
/E (3. Supervision Notes: Supervisees must take supervision notes to maintain an accurate record of their supervision hours. These notes serve as an essential tool for documenting the content and progress of each supervision session, ensuring that the supervisee can integrate the feedback received. Additionally, these records are crucial for evidencing the fulfillment of supervision requirements, whether for certification, accreditation, or professional development. The notes should include a concise summary of the key topics discussed, insights gained, challenges addressed, and any action plans or goals set during the session. Proper documentation not only supports accountability but also aids in the supervisee's professional growth and development as a practitioner. Please refer to the Guidelines for Professional Language; for supervision notes, no academic citation is required and informal language is acceptable, as long as it is clear, respectful, and appropriate. See Appendix 6.5 for a template of Supervision notes.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [10]
>>
