/T (Intervision Guidelines Intervision is a form of peer counseling where three or more counseling professionals come together to discuss cases, share experiences, and provide mutual support and feedback. Its purpose is to enhance professional growth, encourage collaboration, exchange peer review and feedback, and strengthen team dynamics by fostering trust and open communication. Intervision also promotes problem-solving through diverse perspectives, helping participants develop new insights and approaches.)
/E (Intervision Guidelines Intervision is a form of peer counseling where three or more counseling professionals come together to discuss cases, share experiences, and provide mutual support and feedback. Its purpose is to enhance professional growth, encourage collaboration, exchange peer review and feedback, and strengthen team dynamics by fostering trust and open communication. Intervision also promotes problem-solving through diverse perspectives, helping participants develop new insights and approaches.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
