462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (ACT membership offers a number of benefits designed to support and create valuable opportunities for counselors in Thailand: )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (1. Collaboration and Networking: ACT membership gives you the opportunity to meet other counselors, creating opportunities for collaboration, sharing knowledge, gaining support, and mutual learning. Forging connections with other counselors is a great way to learn new things to apply to your own counseling practice, as well as opening doors to potential partnerships and referrals. Additionally, ACT members will gain connections to professional supervisors and experts in the field, helping them enhance their practice with expert guidance. We have regular meetings and events throughout the year to build relationships and expand mental health awareness. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (2. Professional Development: Gain access to workshops, courses, certifications, seminars, and webinars about counseling and mental health that contribute towards your professional development and growth at a discounted rate. These workshops are a great opportunity to improve your knowledge and expand your skills. ACT-approved workshops will count towards your annual continuing professional development \(CPD\) hours.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (3. International Recognition and Potential for Transferable Hours \(TBC\): ACT membership provides a pathway to international recognition, opening doors for practicing counselors to gain credibility across borders. Counseling hours may be transferable across certain countries with similar requirements, allowing members to move forward with their practice when moving to different regions or pursuing further qualifications \(subject to confirmation of transfer agreements\).)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (4. ACT Library: ACT has amassed a large collection of excellent resources in the field of counseling. We are dedicated to raising funds in order to develop a digital library and translate important resources and publications from English to Thai in order to increase accessibility. In the meantime, members will be able to access the physical ACT Library upon request. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (5. Supervision: ACT gives access to a network of qualified Supervisors to support counselors in deepening their understanding of methodologies, discuss challenging cases, and reflect on their personal growth as a mental health professional. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (6. Intervision: ACT provides opportunities for counselors to gather and engage in peer-led support, fostering collaboration, reflection, and team building. Through regular Intervision sessions, members can exchange methods, discuss case studies, and address challenges in a supportive environment. Intervision strengthens professional growth, encourages mutual learning, and promotes a sense of community among counselors.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
469 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (7. Global Mental Health Developments: Stay informed on the latest developments of mental health practices according to international standards so that your own practice is updated to the highest standard of quality. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
